course: dictionary
lesson: 3626
title: Many meanings of find
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Find is a small word with many jobs. It can mean to get something you were looking for, to learn something, or to work out a sum. The words around it tell you which job it is doing.
explain: «To find how many there were at the start, begin at the end and undo each step in the opposite order.» You are not searching for anything here. The words «how many» and «at the start» are clues that find means work out.
explain: «If something ever goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders called the black box help investigators find out why.» Investigators do not go looking for a box to find. Find out means learn, so the clue is the word «out» and the word «why».
explain: Some words feel different, so ask what the sentence is about. «In-laws do not always find long visits easy.» Here find means feel that something is easy or hard. When you are not sure, swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Find» means to see or get something you were looking for, or to come across something by chance.
fact: «Find out» means to learn something, for example to find out the answer.
fact: In maths, «find» means to work out a number, as in «find the missing number» or «find the area».
fact: «A find» is a noun: it is something good that has been found, like a lost ring in the park.
fact: «Finders keepers» is a playground saying that means whoever finds a thing keeps it. It is casual talk, so do not use it in a formal essay.
exercise: «To find how many there were at the start, begin at the end and undo each step.» In this sentence, what does find mean? | Look under the sofa | Paint it | Give up | *Work out
exercise: «In-laws do not always find long visits easy.» What does find mean here? | To lose track of time | *To feel that something is easy or hard | To buy a ticket for a visit | To see a visit in a book
exercise: Which word could replace «find out» in «The black box helps investigators find out why»? | *learn | ignore | lose | forget
test: «Good find!» is said when someone spots something good. In this phrase, what does a find mean? | *Something good that was found | A rude reply | A type of maths sum | A long walk in the woods
test: In maths, «find the area» means what? | Paint the area | Lose the area | *Work out the area | Put the area in a box
exam: In the formal exam voice, which word could replace «find» in «find the missing number»? | forget | lose | *compute | sing
